Correct Filer's chrome, and draw it from the Lucide set

Filer built its own application identity in the title row. The toolkit draws
one for every window now and resolves the application's menu, so the hand-built
copy was a second "Filer" trigger sitting beside back and forward. It is
removed, not hidden.

The sidebar was squished against its own edge: its rows and its section
headings were inset from different origins, so PLACES sat inboard of the rows
it captions. The list now owns 6px and both own 8px inside it.

The view pickers drew their chosen state as ink on ink — a blank block where
the current view should read — and were rounded only at the leading pair. One
of the three asked for view-dual-symbolic, which no installed theme has, so the
Columns picker had nothing to draw at all.

Twenty icons from the simulator's Lucide set ship in Nautilus's own resource
path, answering only for Filer and replacing no icon theme.

The stylesheet corrections carry `window.` before the window class so they hold
wherever they land in the sheet, and sit outside the light-mode block, which the
older Filer rules do not.

